Apart from that, the mysterious force cannot be a compensation for the
chaotic lack of artifacts, for several reasons.
Imprimis, it hits chaotics as well as lawfuls and neutrals. Ok, it hits
chaotics _less_, but they still suffer from it. If it had been merely
compensation for the artifacts, it should not bother chaotics at all.
And it still hits neutrals less than lawfuls; maybe I'm the only one,
but I don't think that getting both Magicbane and Mjollnir is any worse
than just Grayswandir...
Secundis, the common opinion that chaotics get worse toys is not as
correct as it seems. Lawfuls may get Grayswandir, and can dip for
Excalibur; neutrals can get Magicbane and Mjollnir; chaotics can get
Stormbringer, which is not quite as good as GW or MJ, but no dog's
dropping, either. Most importantly, though, chaotics can get Frosty just
as easily as the others, and that's usually seen as the second-best
weapon in the game.
And tertiis, any anti-chaotic imbalance that may exist in the game is
already well compensated for by the lower prayer timeout of chaotics,
which really does affect only them and not neutrals as well.

And finally, imbalance or no, having to tread through level upon level
of mazes that I've already been through four times this game just bores
and irritates me immensely, especially when it's Asmodeus' Grand Tour Of
The Level. That cannot be the intention of a well-balanced game.

